        "original_id": "2a1e54a5-67de-5b54-a8a7-23b6873b3a32",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen Gaghan, Patrick Massett, John Zinman, Steven Soderbergh\n- Films: Gold, Traffic, Syriana\n- Events: Bre-X mining scandal\n- Places: Indonesia\n\nFacts:\n- In 1993, the Bre-X mining scandal involved a supposed discovery of a massive gold deposit in the jungles of Indonesia.\n- The 2016 American crime drama film Gold is loosely based on the 1993 Bre-X mining scandal.\n- For legal reasons and to enhance Gold's appeal, the filmmakers changed character names and story details from the true story.\n- Gold was directed by Stephen Gaghan and written by Patrick Massett and John Zinman.\n- Stephen Gaghan is noted for writing the screenplay for Steven Soderbergh's film Traffic, which was based on a Channel 4 series, and for winning the Academy Award for that screenplay.\n- Stephen Gaghan also wrote and directed Syriana.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
